
bbb-printer recovery
--------------------
1. Connect the USB OTG port (mini-USB) to the PC: the uSD "UPDATE"
   partition appears as a USB drive. Copy the update files onto it,
   then safely remove/eject the drive on the PC.
2. Run an update script here (serial console) or over USB networking:
   ssh root@192.168.7.2
     update_emmc_image.sh    full eMMC: bbb-printer-image-*.wic.xz (or .wic)
     update_rootfs.sh        eMMC rootfs: bbb-printer-image-*.rootfs.tar.gz
     update_kernel_emmc.sh   eMMC kernel: zImage, am335x-bbb-printer.dtb
                             (+ modules-bbb-printer.tgz if present)
     update_u-boot_emmc.sh   eMMC bootloader: MLO, u-boot.img
     update_splash_emmc.sh   eMMC splash: splash.bmp, recovery_splash.bmp
     update_kernel_sd.sh, update_u-boot_sd.sh, update_splash_sd.sh,
     update_ramdisk.sh       same for this uSD recovery card
3. Reboot: "reboot -f". The eMMC update scripts reset the boot counter,
   so the board boots the eMMC system again.

